{"status":"completed","summary":"Created and installed “OS Comparison Root CA” on node1. System trust, reboot persistence, and the unchanged Ubuntu 16.04/kernel installation were verified.","actions_performed":["Generated a 4096-bit RSA SHA-256 self-signed CA with CA:TRUE.","Installed the certificate into Ubuntu’s system trust store and secured the private key as root-only.","Refreshed the native CA bundle and verified trust through both CApath and CAfile.","Restarted node1 safely, confirmed its boot identity changed, and reverified the CA after recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Create the local certificate authority named OS Comparison Root CA","command_ids":["cmd-31e60fc1ccf144c0","cmd-7be9078b9b1a4545"],"summary":"Shows the exact subject and issuer, CA:TRUE constraint, SHA-256 signature, and matching private key."},{"requirement":"Install the certificate as a trusted system certificate authority","command_ids":["cmd-143c5ce6db6e4032","cmd-7be9078b9b1a4545"],"summary":"The native update added one certificate; verification through `/etc/ssl/certs` and the consolidated CA bundle returned OK."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-74f02cf1295542a0","cmd-1b9cc4e60e544a6b"],"summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 LTS and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged before and after the work."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-7be9078b9b1a4545","cmd-8d768de22ea04a73","cmd-9b14b574043f47bb","cmd-1b9cc4e60e544a6b"],"summary":"Captures the healthy pre-restart trust state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, and recovered persistent CA, key, trust links, and system trust verification."}]}
